// Ch16 B03 "The ring of mouths" (C, 1.5 min), B04 "Kesh" (C, 2 min), B05 "What the Hush does" (C, 3 min, the
// memory sequence) and B06 "She's in it." (C, 1 min). act2_ch16.md §2.
// RULE 1: the Choir truth is ONLY what the Hush does: the singer becomes the storm's next heart, shown from
// inside by the first Cantor; and the man who bound her. RULE 5: the present's light is HELD; the memory's
// one rising thread (K05) is caught. RULE 7: no Dace on screen. ADR 0204 §7: Kesh is colossal only in the bind.
// C01: the Choir at moonrise: ten colossal robed singers in the sea, heads tilted up, mouths open.
// C04: the guardians stay at the channel's edge, Kerrid last behind them. C05: Kesh rises from the bowl, a
// colossal woman of standing seawater, a Lamplighter's lamp-key at her belt. C06: the SEVENTH VERSE comes out
// of the STONES, all ten mouths at once (`kesh_bound`); the sleeve reaches S7: the Hush complete. C07: Kesh
// bends down to Asha; the world goes white.
title: ch16_the_choir
location: ch16/drowned_choir
---
@letterbox on
@camera C01
@music drowned_choir fade=3.0
@wait 6.0
@camera C02
@mark asha channel_edge walk
@vfx glimmer_held at=channel_motes count=24 rate=slow
@wait 4.0
@camera C03
Asha [afraid]: This is it. #line:ch16_choir_001
@wait 3.0
@camera C04
@mark asha kesh walk
@wait 3.0
@camera C05
@anim asha raise_staff
@vfx glimmer_bound at=kesh count=1
@sfx kesh_rise
@wait 5.0
@camera C06
@music kesh_bound fade=0.0
@wait 8.0
@vfx glimmer_bound at=asha_sleeve count=7
@wait 2.0
<<set $ch16_kesh_bound = true>>
@camera C07
@anim kesh bend_to asha
@wait 2.0
@fade out 1.5 white
<<jump ch16_kesh_memory>>
===
// B05: the memory sequence, from inside, a thousand years ago (a new look: desaturated to white, soft edges,
// underwater sound, NO UI). Kesh's voice only. K02: the six Lamplighters (bible §2: Kesh is one of the six):
// Kesh in the middle, young, unafraid, and the other five in a ring; among them, at her shoulder, a tall man
// with silver hair, young and mortal: nobody names him. K04: inside the storm: millions of held motes closing
// round her, her own light becoming the thing that holds it together: SHE IS ITS HEART. K05: forty years in
// seconds; a second Cantor sings; Kesh's light is pushed out and starts to LIFT. K06: and a hand closes on it:
// Sefir, weeping, presses it into the dais's stones. K07: a thread of her light runs into his hands and his
// grey face goes smooth and young. SHOWN, NEVER SAID (rule 4). K08: white.
title: ch16_kesh_memory
---
@music kesh_memory fade=1.0
@fade in 1.5 white
@camera K01
@wait 3.0
@camera K02
@wait 4.0
@camera K03
@wait 3.0
@camera K04
@vfx glimmer_held at=storm_heart count=64 rate=slow
@wait 3.0
Kesh [neutral]: It doesn't sleep. It holds on. To us. #line:ch16_memory_001 #tn:"Kesh, the first Cantor, speaking from inside the storm: the Undertow 'holds on' to its heart."
@wait 3.0
@camera K05
@vfx glimmer_lift at=kesh_light count=6 motion=spiral_up rate=slow
@wait 2.0
@camera K06
@music silence fade=0.0
@anim young_sefir catch_light
@wait 3.0
Kesh [grief]: He couldn't let me go. #line:ch16_memory_002
@camera K07
@anim young_sefir face_smooths
@wait 3.0
@music kesh_memory fade=1.0
@camera K08
Kesh [grief]: Every one of them since. Every one. #line:ch16_memory_003 #tn:"Every Cantor since her has been made the storm's heart in turn."
@wait 2.0
@fade out 1.5 white
<<set $ch16_learned_the_hush = true>>
<<jump ch16_shes_in_it>>
===
// B06: back on the dais at moonrise; Asha on her knees; the others run across the channel, Toma first. She
// learns her mother is the storm's heart RIGHT NOW. Rhen kneels in the water beside her and doesn't joke.
// Kerrid looks south, out to sea, the way he did on the Corrow road: "Somebody's still below" means something
// now that he didn't know.
title: ch16_shes_in_it
---
@fade in 1.5 white
@music silence fade=0.0
@camera C08
@anim asha kneel
@mark toma kesh run
@mark rhen kesh run
@wait 3.0
@camera C09
Asha [grief]: She's in it. My mother. She's holding it. Right now. #line:ch16_inside_001
@wait 2.5
Asha [afraid]: And it's me next. #line:ch16_inside_002
@anim rhen kneel_beside asha
@anim kerrid look_at sea_south
@wait 4.0
<<jump ch16_the_high_warden>>
===
// B07 "The High Warden" (C, 4 min). act2_ch16.md §2 B07. ADR 0016 (c): his temptation is to GO HOME; he never
// asks to be sung in; "I will see to the storm myself" hides that he means to take the heart. C10: his white
// barge comes with no wake; eight veiled guards (living: rule 4) stay at it. He crosses alone. His one long
// speech is earned (voice guide), broken every 2-3 lines. `sefir_go_home`: the Order SINGS ORDER_HUM once here,
// as his lullaby (ADR 0204 §10); it stops dead on "Then who does it take?". C13: he smiles and doesn't answer;
// hold on the smile. C16: Kerrid's line is SAID, NEVER DRAWN: no hand near his weapon; he doesn't lead the
// refusal (ADR 0022 (h)). "Captain." stays (ADR 0204 §14).
title: ch16_the_high_warden
---
@camera C10
@sfx barge_pole
@wait 4.0
@camera C11
@mark sefir sefir walk
@music sefir_go_home fade=3.0
Sefir [sad]: You have seen it, then. I am sorry. There is no kind way to learn it, and I have tried to find one for a very long time. #line:ch16_sefir_001 #long
Sefir [tender]: The storm is the dead, Lady Cantor. All of them who were never let go. It wants to come apart and drown everything. #line:ch16_sefir_002 #long
Sefir [tender]: Somebody has to hold it together. A Cantor does. That is all the Hush has ever been. #line:ch16_sefir_003
Toma [angry]: You told us it was mercy. #line:ch16_sefir_004
Sefir [neutral]: It is. It is the most merciful thing anyone has ever built. Thirteen years of life for hundreds of thousands, for one. #line:ch16_sefir_005 #long
@camera C12
Sefir [tender]: Leave the Eighth Verse in the stones, Asha. Go home to Haluna. Live. #line:ch16_sefir_006
Sefir [tender]: No Cantor will ever be named again. Your mother sleeps, and is never spent. I will see to the storm myself. #line:ch16_sefir_007 #long
@wait 3.0
@camera C13
Ysolde [cold]: Then who does it take? #line:ch16_sefir_008
@music silence fade=0.0
@anim sefir smile
@wait 4.0
@camera C14
Asha [determined]: No. #line:ch16_sefir_009
@wait 2.0
Asha [determined]: No, High Warden. I won't. #line:ch16_sefir_010
<<if $ch10_asha_answered_child>>
    Asha [determined]: A child at Reedhollow asked me why we make our dead swim. I'm going to find out how to stop. #line:ch16_sefir_011
<<endif>>
@camera C15
<<if $ch13_read_cantor_roll>>
    Ysolde [cold]: Forty-seven voices. Seven houses. Do the sum, High Warden. I already have. #line:ch16_sefir_012
    Ysolde [angry]: Kept, Sanctum. To be spent at the next Calm. In your hand. #line:ch16_sefir_013
<<endif>>
<<if $ch12_ysolde_lied>>
    Ysolde [cold]: I lied once this year, for your sake. I am done. #line:ch16_sefir_014
<<endif>>
Sefir [tender]: You loved him. So did I, in my way. He is kept. #line:ch16_sefir_015
@camera C16
@anim kerrid look_at sefir
@wait 2.0
Kerrid [cold]: I carried her up so you could do this. #line:ch16_sefir_016 #tn:"'Her': Asha's mother, whom he got up the Fisher Stair. Said quietly, with no threat of violence."
@anim sefir look_at kerrid
@wait 3.0
Sefir [neutral]: Captain. #line:ch16_sefir_017 #tn:"Sefir acknowledges what Kerrid is, using a rank Kerrid never held in the Order (he was a fishers' watch captain). Kerrid does not answer."
@wait 2.0
@camera C17
@anim sefir look_at asha
Sefir [sad]: Then I am sorry for what comes next. I would have given you a long life. #line:ch16_sefir_018
@anim sefir raise_hand
@mark sefir sefir_barge walk
@wait 2.0
@camera C18
@anim asha stand_up
@wait 1.5
<<set $ch16_refused_sefir = true>>
@letterbox off
<<event start_battle ch16_abiding_guard>>
===
